  "source": { "doc": "mk60.pdf", "page": "9 and 10", "section": "Ordering Schematic with the spring ranges and Cv tables" },
  "note": "Extracted by hand from the ordering schematic. Four models on one sheet: 60 standard, 60HP high pressure, 60QC quick change and 61 large diaphragm. Held for John, three extraction points: (1) the schematic header row in this extraction prints no separators, where the Mark 50 sheet prints model dash size dash body slash, so this code assembles bare and wants checking against the PDF; (2) the F1 end prints 125# IFE against its own except-IFE bracket, an artefact read as 125# FE to match the F series pattern and the Mark 50 sheet; (3) the DIN end rows sit between the two end-connection lists in the extraction with their own DN15-150 span, so they are carried once, from 1/2 inch up, for carbon and stainless bodies as their bracket says. The spring tables are printed for 60 and 60QC together, for 60HP and for 61, banded by size; the 60QC column is not separately distinguished, so it rides the 60 table, held for John. The Cv ladder is constrained per size from the Cv values and maximum differential pressures table, downward only, per the low flow note. The prose options, grain processing and cryogenic housing, have no schematic position and so no place in the code.",
